Pumping Efficiency - Simply stated, the Pumping Efficiency measures the flow losses thru the intake, ports, and valves. For example, if a 2.2L engine has a PumpEff of 80% @ 3000rpm, it will pump 2.2 * 0.8 = 1.76L per revolution. The Pumping Efficiency is very similar to the";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:1:{s:13:"template_file";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:8:"shelgame";s:9:"Rob Lloyd";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1421461383;s:8:"modified";i:1422804216;}s:11:"last_change";a:7:{s:4:"date";i:1422804216;s:2:"ip";s:13:"23.115.161.12";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:8:"glossary";s:4:"user";s:8:"shelgame";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:8:"shelgame";s:9:"Rob Lloyd";}}}